# TypeScript / JavaScript — Expert Foundational Skill

Expert TypeScript and modern JavaScript conventions. Apply to all TS/JS work across any framework.

---

## TypeScript Configuration

### Strict tsconfig.json
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true,
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  }
}
```

> **Caveats:**
> - `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` can break some third-party library typings — enable and fix errors rather than disabling
> - `moduleResolution: "bundler"` requires a bundler (Next.js, Vite, etc.) — for pure Node.js scripts use `"node16"` or `"nodenext"` instead
> - `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` is stricter than most libraries expect — may require `// @ts-expect-error` on some external types

